# The kit ref this repository runs. One line: a 40-character commit
# sha, or a v<semver> tag. NEVER a branch.
#
# THIS IS origin/master's sha AND NOT kit's local HEAD, and the difference is the
# whole reason the value was taken the way it was. kit's checkout on this machine
# was AHEAD of its remote when this was written, so pinning local HEAD would name
# a commit that exists on exactly one laptop: every other developer's `git fetch`
# of that sha fails, and the failure names a sha rather than a ref, which is the
# worst way for a pin to break. A pin whose value is not fetchable is not a pin;
# it is a claim about a machine.
d3d56f7a2e781186d46cdd8fcf735712940dcc97
